   "date": "2015-12-19T15:02:15Z",
   "subject": "Re: GAM ggplot",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif\">My recommendation would be to avoid the `qplot()` function and switch to `ggplot()`.</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif\">Something along the lines of:</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\"><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">ggplot(AbuAfiMz, aes(x = TEPais, y = AbuAfiMz)) +</font></div><div class=\"gmail_default\"><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">   theme_bw() +</font></div><div class=\"gmail_default\"><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">   geom_point() +</font></div><div class=\"gmail_default\"><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">   geom_smooth(method = &quot;gam&quot;, formula = y ~ s(x))</font></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif\">Cheers,</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms,sans-serif\">Roman</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
